<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Taizu of Liao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">872–<a href="/years/926">926</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Yelü Abaoji, Abaoji · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yelü Abaoji, Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song">Taizu</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a>, was the Khitan leader who founded the Liao dynasty. Chosen as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a> around 907, he broke with the custom of rotating leadership, proclaimed himself emperor in 916 and built a state combining steppe and Chinese institutions, including a Khitan script. He conquered the kingdom of Balhae in 926 and died on the way home.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>When the Khitan armies of <b>Yelü Abaoji</b> invaded in 925, Balhae's frontier fortresses and capital fell within weeks, suggesting that the kingdom's military strength had declined during the long peace.</blockquote><a href="/empire/balhae">Balhae · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Traditionally in 907, as the Tang dynasty collapsed, <b>Abaoji</b> of the Yila tribe and the Yelü clan was chosen as khagan.</blockquote><a href="/empire/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Abaoji</b>, the Khitan leader later known as Emperor Taizu of Liao, became khagan of the Khitans.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/february-27">27 February in history</a></li><li><blockquote>In 926 <b>Abaoji</b>, founder of the Liao dynasty, destroyed Balhae after a short campaign and took its capital Huhan (Holhan).</blockquote><a href="/state/dongdan">Dongdan</a></li></ul></section>
